      "start": 0.34,
      "end": 1.55,
      "text": "Hey there, how are you?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 11.69,
      "end": 16.5,
      "text": "Totally normal worry. How far is the trip, and what's your car's real range in practice?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 23.28,
      "end": 30.17,
      "text": "Then plan on two charging stops, maybe three to be relaxed. A route planning app can show fast chargers along the way."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 33.61,
      "end": 42.36,
      "text": "On a fast charger, usually twenty to forty minutes to get from low to about eighty percent. Charging slows down a lot after that, so it's rarely worth waiting for full."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 48.29,
      "end": 54.19,
      "text": "That's why it's good to arrive at each stop with some buffer, and have a backup charger in mind nearby."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 63.24,
      "end": 67.138,
      "text": "Exactly, line the stops up with meals and it barely feels like waiting."
    }
